<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Frederick, Margrave of Baden-Durlach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1573">1573</a>–<a href="/years/1638">1638</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Frederick was Margrave of Baden-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durlach">Durlach</a> from 1604 to 1622, a Protestant prince and military writer. To fight for the Protestant cause in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War he handed the government to his son in 1622, but was defeated by Tilly at Wimpfen that year. He spent his last years in exile and died in Strasbourg in 1638.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-frederick-margrave-of-baden-durlach.jpg" alt="George Frederick, Margrave of Baden-Durlach" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Philipp Kilian / Johann Kaspar Widmann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Friedrich_V_Baden-Durlach.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
